      "writtenOn": "2026-05-11T15:13:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So we will be sending seed, and random_seed if both set, unless dont send members if NULL is enabled in json serializer.  When we start playing around with serializers I believe its time we use some polymorphism here and we are clear on construction what we are expecting instead of this grey area.\n\nI think we should introduce a new AIChatCompletionRequest remove seed and randomSeed, and place these into 3 new classes:\n AIChatCompletionRequestNoSeed, \n AIChatCompletionRequestSeed\n AIChatCompletionRequestRandomSeed.  \n \nWe need a new factory class to create this which uses aiType to switch as before and return either one of these new concrete types.  The interface / base class should define methods for getSeed -\u003e note do not call this getRandomSeed, then the implementation can be overriden in the NoSeed to return null, seed, or randomSeed as each override class requires.   This allows this to grow and be reused, but most importantly its not specific to MISTRAL.  As there are other providers that need positive only seeds, or to use seed/random_seed in the serialized info.",
      "revId": "dc05bc5f66c8726ff3ef2949ab14cb1f4edfde9c",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
